- rewarding / motivation system (keep students consistent in homework, training, recitation):
  - goal: encourage consistency without shaming laggards; derive everything from
    data the bot already records so students do nothing extra.
  - data sources (already tracked, no new student input):
    - `homework_submissions` → submitted per member (review/resubmit are
      teacher-followup states, not rewarded).
    - `session_participants.attendance_status` (present/listening/excused/absent)
      joined with `sessions.session_type` → attendance across main / training /
      recitation (recitation is rewarded via attendance, not page counts).
    - `member_progress` (pages/verse) → recitation progress for tracking, not scoring.
  - phase 1 — حسنات points (MVP):
    - [ ] define a points config (homework submitted, attendance by status
      × session-type weight) with `main` weighted highest, then `training`, then
      the recitation family. Ships as hardcoded `DEFAULT_POINTS`.
    - [ ] add a scoring module that aggregates points per member per course cycle
      from the existing tables (no schema change; pure read/aggregate).
    - [ ] make the points config editable per class (teacher overrides stored on
      `group_settings`, merged over `DEFAULT_POINTS`; add a /manage editor with
      reset-to-default). Depends on the points config + scoring module.
    - [ ] surface a "المواظبة" section: warm, collective framing
      («الأكثر مواظبة هذا الأسبوع»), never shaming.
  - phase 2 — positive nudges (reuse `lib/pendingNudge.js`):
    - [ ] auto-congratulate completers in the homework group
      («ما شاء الله، أتممتِ تكاليف الأسبوع»).
    - [ ] gentle private reminder to those falling behind (opt-in / admin toggle).
  - phase 3 — streaks & badges (personal progress, everyone can win):
    - [ ] per-member streak counter (e.g. consecutive weeks with no missed
      homework), resets on a miss.
    - [ ] milestone badges/أوسمة (first homework reviewed, full month attendance,
      recitation page target). needs a small `member_rewards` table (idempotent
      migration + supabase_v2.sql update).
  - [ ] phase 4 — tiers/levels (optional): map cumulative points to named tiers
    (مجتهدة → متميّزة → متقنة) for long-term goals without direct ranking.
  - [ ] phase 5 — image reports: render the weekly "المواظبة" summary via the render
    engine (`lib/render/`) instead of plain text (ties into "generate nice reports").
  - recommended start: phase 1 (points from existing data) + phase 2 (positive
    nudges), shown as a weekly image summary.